{"id": "EUVD-2026-86681", "enisaUuid": "4db6435a-7323-3afd-a8ed-2fc0d1c6fe3d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\neth: nfp: drop the replaced rule from the list when reprogramming fails\n\nnfp_net_fs_add() replaces an existing rule by deleting it from the\nhardware, decrementing nn->fs.count and programming the new one.  If\nnfp_net_fs_add_hw() fails the old entry stays on nn->fs.list - only the\nsuccess path reaches list_replace() - so the list is one longer than\nnn->fs.count, and it advertises a rule whose hardware entry has already\nbeen torn down.\n\nnn->fs.count is what ETHTOOL_GRXCLSRLCNT reports, so userspace then sizes\nits buffer one entry short of what the GRXCLSRLALL walk wants to write.\nThat used to overwrite one u32 past the allocation; since the walk is\nbounded it is a permanent -EMSGSIZE instead, as nothing ever resyncs the\ncounter.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:12:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/603b70093f729f52a37544b48679903cad834856", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/edaec279f59f801a05b751df475ed71a0a68c88a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/552e528a7d85cbe088b2ae4f78194713975b46cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/108bb2142e3a12c9ad625ad662973127a113ddc6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98028", "GHSA-9537-hf5q-v67h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "66c1eb86-62d3-34a7-beb6-a3b9015aecb1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9eb03bb1c035ff6e2c3a34046419446588253dda <552e528a7d85cbe088b2ae4f78194713975b46cf"}, {"id": "6e35a930-4512-3951-9fca-292ce49b258c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9eb03bb1c035ff6e2c3a34046419446588253dda <edaec279f59f801a05b751df475ed71a0a68c88a"}, {"id": "7996ca51-e9ae-3493-be19-4d270598a75a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9eb03bb1c035ff6e2c3a34046419446588253dda <603b70093f729f52a37544b48679903cad834856"}, {"id": "7d0f1df2-1a1e-3a12-94d9-96bf019b35af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "827579f3-7c02-3204-8085-41ed97d86d1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "ace59fb3-c8bd-33c6-b1e7-6ef4ec7dfd5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "d1b92983-e8f1-3a44-8513-e091ebf471c2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "e77bd92d-a147-3b80-bd65-4542e1d91239", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e9d60fc9-8682-3e0e-a193-c4e15acf65c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9eb03bb1c035ff6e2c3a34046419446588253dda <108bb2142e3a12c9ad625ad662973127a113ddc6"}, {"id": "efbba3fe-c19e-349c-8141-f0bbc4392def", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0bb9d065-1d11-3f29-843a-85c336f51030", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}